---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const tracks = [
  { title: "AI infrastructure", slug: "ai-infrastructure", build: "An inference gateway", text: "Stream model responses, manage admission, and measure latency and throughput." },
  { title: "Storage engines", slug: "storage-engines", build: "A distributed key-value store", text: "Build an LSM-tree engine and prove recovery after crashes and partitions." },
  { title: "Cloud & network", slug: "cloud-and-network", build: "A programmable edge proxy", text: "Route traffic through a Rust proxy and reload it without dropping active requests." },
];
---
<Base title="The Blueprint">
  <div class="home">
    <section class="home-intro" aria-labelledby="home-heading">
      <div class="home-copy">
        <h1 id="home-heading">Build the systems<br />behind the service.</h1>
        <p class="home-lede">Start with a Go service. Build a Rust data plane, connect them over Linux sockets, then ship a system you can test and explain.</p>
        <div class="home-actions">
          <a class="home-primary" href="/1-foundations/01-set-up-your-machine/">Start Foundations</a>
          <a href="/journey/">Explore the curriculum</a>
        </div>
        <p class="home-entry">Already code? <a href="/1-foundations/test-out/">Take the test-out</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="switchyard">
        <figcaption><strong>Switchyard</strong><span>Core project</span></figcaption>
        <div class="switchyard-flow">
          <div class="switchyard-node">
            <span class="node-language">GO</span>
            <strong>Control plane</strong>
            <span>HTTP, jobs, Raft</span>
          </div>
          <div class="switchyard-wire"><span>TCP / Unix socket</span></div>
          <div class="switchyard-node data-node">
            <span class="node-language">RUST</span>
            <strong>Data plane</strong>
            <span>Frames, buffers, durable log</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="switchyard-foot"><span>Runs on Linux</span><a href="/2-core/01-go-runtime-and-reliable-services/">View the first module</a></div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="route-heading" id="full-route">
      <header class="home-section-heading">
        <h2 id="route-heading">The learning path</h2>
        <a href="/journey/">Full roadmap</a>
      </header>
      <ol class="home-path">
        <li><a href="/1-foundations/01-set-up-your-machine/"><strong>Foundations</strong><span>Go, Python, Linux, and networking from the beginning.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/2-core/01-go-runtime-and-reliable-services/"><strong>Core</strong><span>Build and test Switchyard across eight modules.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="#tracks"><strong>Specialize</strong><span>Pick a track and ship a benchmarked capstone.</span></a></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="tracks-heading" id="tracks">
      <header class="home-section-heading">
        <h2 id="tracks-heading">Choose your track</h2>
      </header>
      <ul class="home-tracks">
        {tracks.map((track) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/3-tracks/${track.slug}/`}>
              <span>{track.title}</span>
              <h3>{track.build}</h3>
              <p>{track.text}</p>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section home-practice" id="try-it" aria-labelledby="practice-heading">
      <div>
        <h2 id="practice-heading">Put a system under load.</h2>
        <p>Change the arrival rate in the queue simulator and see what happens to wait time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="home-actions">
        <a class="home-primary" href="/labs/queue/">Try the queue lab</a>
        <a href="/labs/">Browse all labs</a>
        <a href="/system-design/interview-rehearsal/">Interview rehearsal</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
